10
00:40:54,545 --> 00:41:00,545
Heavy Metal is a 1981 Canadian adult animated science fantasy anthology film directed by Gerald Potterton (in his directorial debut) and
produced by Ivan Reitman and Leonard Mogel, who also was the publisher of Heavy Metal magazine, which was the basis for the film.

11
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
It starred the voices of Rodger Bumpass, Jackie Burroughs, John Candy, Joe Flaherty, Don Francks, Martin Lavut, Marilyn Lightstone, Eugene Levy,
Alice Playten, Harold Ramis, Percy Rodriguez, Susan Roman, Richard Romanus, August Schellenberg, John Vernon, and Zal Yanovsky.

12
00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
The screenplay was written by Daniel Goldberg and Len Blum.

13
00:53:10,909 --> 00:53:16,909
The film is an anthology of various science-fiction and fantasy stories tied together
by a single theme of an evil force that is "the sum of all evils".

14
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
It was adapted from Heavy Metal magazine and
original stories in the same spirit.

15
01:01:21,818 --> 01:01:27,818
Like the magazine, the film features a great deal of
graphic violence, sexuality, and nudity.

16
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
Its production was expedited by having several animation houses
working simultaneously on different segments.

17
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:38,727
Upon release, the film received mixed reviews from critics, but was a moderate
commercial success and has since achieved a cult following.

18
01:13:38,181 --> 01:13:44,181
Its soundtrack was packaged by music manager Irving Azoff and included several popular rock bands and artists, including Black
Sabbath, Blue Öyster Cult, Sammy Hagar, Don Felder, Cheap Trick, DEVO, Journey, and Nazareth, among others.

19
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
A sequel, Heavy Metal 2000, was released in 2000.

20
01:21:49,090 --> 01:21:55,090
The film explores themes of flying car, taxi, heavy
metal, based on comic, drug use.

21
01:25:54,545 --> 01:26:00,545
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
